  "custom_logic_notes": "Multi-timeframe scoring system: 3 TFs x 5 SMA periods + 2 AC indicators. Each SMA contributes 1 point if rising (bullish) or 1 if falling (bearish). AC contributes 3 points for strong momentum, 0 otherwise. Max raw score per TF = 8 (5 MA + 3 AC), scaled to 0-100 by *12.5. Long signal requires all 3 TF bullish scores > OpenLevel threshold (50 or 75). Short signal requires all 3 TF bearish scores > OpenLevel threshold. AC interpretation is non-trivial: strong bullish = (histogram ascending 3 bars AND below zero AND current > prev) OR (positive AND ascending); strong bearish is the mirror. Neutral AC = mixed/transitioning patterns. OpenLevel/CloseLevel parameters gate signal strength: 0=weak signal accepted, 1=strong signal required. CloseLevel=2 disables signal-based closing.",
